{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792190189,"nonce":"+1AGTFtGQqXi7tVz1Pb8jCjGkdQ=","title":"Haxelib READMEs keep relative links that lead nowhere on Haxelib's page","message":"**What happens**\n\n`scripts/package_haxelib.py` rewrote only `docs/images/...` image paths to raw GitHub URLs. Every other relative reference stayed as written, and Haxelib shows the README on its own site, where a path into the repository resolves to nothing. The main README's `[Visual debugging](docs/debugging.md)` was already broken on Haxelib, and the README banner adds links to `canvaskit/README.md` and `tools/snapshot/scenes/Banner.hx`.\n\n**Fix**\n\n- Rewrite every relative reference outside code blocks and spans: inline Markdown links and images, reference definitions, and HTML `src`, `href` and `poster`. Images and video go to raw.githubusercontent.com so they display; other files go to their page on GitHub (folders to `/tree/`), keeping any `#fragment`. A target that does not exist fails the packaging.\n- Fail packaging if anything relative is left after rewriting.\n- `publish_haxelib.py` checks each archive's README the same way before submitting, since it can publish an older release's archives.\n\n**Tests**\n\ntests/package_haxelib_test.py covers each kind of reference, code left untouched, fragments kept, a missing target, and that every packaged README has nothing relative left. tests/publish_haxelib_test.py checks that a relative README link blocks publication. Both run in ci.yml, and release.yml runs the packaging test before it builds the archives.","files":null}]}